              {
                "rank": 2,
                "score": -1.0361328125,
                "vectorScore": 0.6545408368110657,
                "sourceId": "retail.reports",
                "documentId": "retail.reports:f-ec81cf489eedf143",
                "chunkId": "retail.reports:f-ec81cf489eedf143:0006",
                "title": "regional-performance-q3-2026.pdf",
                "url": null,
                "publishedAt": null,
                "snippet": "Regional Performance Report, Q3 2026\nNet sales by region, $ thousands\nQ3 2025\nQ3 2026\n80\n60\n57.4\n40\n20\n0\nNortheast\nSoutheast\nMidwest\nWest\nE-commerce\nNortheast was the growth leader at +14.4%. West followed at +3.5%, and E-commerce at +3.4%. E-commerce, which is reported as its own region, accounted for 27.7% of net sales. Southeast fell short of the chain at -12.4%; regional operations will review its promotion calendar and Q4 labor plan before the holiday season.",
