                "snippet": "Regional Performance Report, Q3 2026\nStore results\nThe five physical stores with the highest Q3 net sales are shown below. E-commerce is excluded from the ranking because it is not a store. The four flagship stores (S01, S07, S13 and S21) together produced 37.7% of physical store net sales.\nTable 2. Five physical stores with the highest Q3 2026 net sales\n1, Store ID = S21. 1, Store = San Francisco Union Square. 1, Region = West. 1, Net sales = $19,982. 1, Orders = 94. 1, Return rate = 6.8%. 2, Store ID = S13. 2, Store = Chicago Loop. 2, Region = Midwest. 2, Net sales = $15,651. 2, Orders = 74. 2, Return rate = 12.5%. 3, Store ID = S07. 3, Store = Atlanta Midtown. 3, Region = Southeast. 3, Net sales = $12,374. 3, Orders = 57. 3, Return rate = 6.1%. 4, Store ID = S06. 4, Store = Newark Gateway. 4, Region = Northeast. 4, Net sales = $10,911. 4, Orders = 49. 4, Return rate = 10.4%. 5, Store ID = S01. 5, Store = Boston Seaport. 5, Region = Northeast. 5, Net sales = $8,413. 5, Orders = 46. 5, Return rate = 2.7%\nThe newest store, Denver Cherry Creek (S24), opened on August 15, 2025. It delivered $2,160 in net sales in Q3 2026, against $840 in Q3 2025, when it traded for only six weeks.\nRPT-REG-2026Q3 | Version 1.0 Internal use only. Synthetic document for a software demonstration. Page 2 of 4",
